  "summary_md": "The entertainment and broadcasting universe is being reshaped by contrasting forces: AI‑driven content monetization, physical media revivals, and transformative M&A sit alongside persistent advertising headwinds in legacy radio and TV. Cineverse (CNVS) stands out after its acquisitions of IndiCue and Giant Worldwide outperformed expectations, shifting the story toward an AI‑enabled studio with improving analyst sentiment. Angel Studios (ANGX) turned profitable through spending discipline and a fast‑growing guild membership base, while Allied Gaming (AGAE) – fresh off a legal settlement – is pivoting aggressively into an untested crypto and AI narrative with no demonstrated operating record. Elsewhere, consolidation is a clear thread: fuboTV (FUBO) closed its Hulu + Live TV combination and is pushing toward profitability, Gray Media (GTN) is funding an acquisition via a notes offering, and Reservoir Media (RSVR) continues catalog bolt‑ons. Meanwhile, names dependent on traditional advertising face sustained pressure, with iHeartMedia (IHRT) balancing digital growth against a fragile balance sheet, and Urban One (UONE, UONEK) and E.W. Scripps (SSP) grappling with linear ad erosion despite targeted cost and balance‑sheet actions. A secondary theme involves licensing content libraries for AI training (CuriosityStream, CURI) and leveraging physical‑media collector demand (Alliance Entertainment, AENT), underscoring the mix of speculative repositioning and operational turnarounds in the batch.",
